  "nl_text": "The rschema_0164 database contains six tables, each with its own unique purpose. The Warehouse table stores information about the physical location of the warehouse, including its name, location, description, and image. The User table contains information about the users who interact with the warehouse, including their email, phone number, role, and username. The Stack_Position table stores information about the specific locations within the warehouse, such as the type of stack, the location of the stack, and the description of the stack. The Sensor table stores information about the sensors that are used to monitor the stacks, including the type of sensor, the data it collects, and the status of the sensor. The User_Operation_Stack_Position table stores information about the operations that are performed on the stacks, including the type of operation, the time of the operation, and the user who performed the operation. Finally, the Stack_Position_Alert table stores information about any alerts that are triggered by the sensors, including the type of alert, the level of the alert, and the time of the alert. Each table is linked to the others through foreign keys, ensuring that the data is consistent and accurate.",
  "gold_question": "The Tobacco Storage Monitoring and Maintenance Data Management System primarily implements the following functionalities:\n1.Warehouse Information Management: Manages the information related to each warehouse, including Warehouse Name, Warehouse Location, Warehouse Type, Warehouse Image Path, Warehouse Description, Creation Time, Creation Date, and Update Date.\n2.Stack Position Information Management: Manages the information related to each stack position, including Stack Position Name, Stack Position Type, Stack Position Image Path, Stack Position Description, Creation Time, Creation Date, and Update Date. Each stack position belongs to a specific warehouse.\n3.Sensor Management: Sensors placed in the warehouse and tobacco stacks collect real-time environmental parameters such as temperature, humidity, box temperature, and oxygen concentration. Collected information includes Sensor Type, Collected Data Value, Collection Time, Data Status, and Data Description.\n4.User Management: Registers unique information for each user, including Username, User Role, User Password, User Phone, User Email, Creation Time, Creation Date, and Update Date.\n5.Dynamic Monitoring and Risk Alerts: Each user can perform actions on stack positions and records the Operation Type, Operation Time, and Operation Description. Each stack position is monitored by sensors, and alerts are issued based on the monitoring indicators, recording Alert Type, Alert Time, Alert Level, Alert Description, and Alert Status.\n\nThe design takes into account multiple aspects such as warehouse, stack position, sensor data, operation records, user information, and alert information to support comprehensive system management and data security needs.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0164.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0164\nCREATE TABLE `warehouse` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stack_position` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `warehouse_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stack_position_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`warehouse_id`) REFERENCES `warehouse` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sensor` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `stack_position_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `data_collected` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sensor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`stack_position_id`) REFERENCES `stack_position` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_operation_stack_position` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stack_position_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_operation_stack_position_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_operation_stack_position_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`stack_position_id`) REFERENCES `stack_position` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stack_position_alert` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `alert_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `alert_level` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `alert_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stack_position_alert_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sensor_id`) REFERENCES `sensor` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
